Title:
PLATINUMPICK — Windows Kernel-Mode Shellcode Development Framework (WKMSDF)

Type:
GitHub Tool

Short Summary (4-8 sentences max):
PLATINUMPICK is a C++20 framework for authoring Windows x64 kernel-mode position-independent code (PIC) / shellcode. It provides conventions and helper macros to avoid common PIC pitfalls (no globals, stack-based strings) and to resolve kernel exports at runtime via manual PE parsing rather than static imports. The framework includes a method to locate the ntoskrnl.exe base address using IDT “scandown,” then dynamically resolves functions like `DbgPrint`. It emphasizes safe execution constraints such as requiring the payload to run at IRQL 0 (PASSIVE_LEVEL), suggesting work items or passive-level DPCs. It’s primarily useful for red teamers, exploit developers, and kernel security researchers building or testing ring-0 payloads, and it also highlights defensive mitigations (HVCI, WDAC) relevant to blue teams. The repo is designed around a MinGW-w64 + GNU Make toolchain under MSYS2, with VS Code as the editor workflow.

Technical Focus:
- Windows x64 kernel-mode PIC/shellcode in C++20
- Runtime dynamic linking of kernel exports (manual PE export parsing)
- Locating `ntoskrnl.exe` base via IDT scandown
- IRQL/PASSIVE_LEVEL execution requirements (work items, passive-level DPCs)
- Stack strings / avoiding global state for PIC safety
- Testing via FLARE `kscldr` kernel shellcode loader

Use Cases:
- Develop and compile custom Windows kernel-mode shellcode payloads
- Prototype ring-0 post-exploitation actions with minimal dependencies/imports
- Research kernel export resolution and KASLR-aware base discovery techniques
- Validate kernel shellcode behavior in a VM using `flare-kscldr` + kernel debugging
- Build PoCs for vulnerable-driver-assisted kernel code execution scenarios

Keywords:
Windows kernel, ring 0, kernel-mode shellcode, PIC, position-independent code, C++20, x64, ntoskrnl.exe, IDT scandown, KASLR, IRQL, PASSIVE_LEVEL, DPC, work item, manual PE parsing, export resolution, DbgPrint, MinGW-w64, MSYS2, WDAC, HVCI, Intel EPT, MBEC, FLARE kscldr